                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">5dc7211f-77cb-4ab8-aba8-3b0efa80795e</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Parameter value sources</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Instead of a fixed value, a Parameter Value can get its value from a source, evaluated in the App when the export is triggered:

- Screenshot Source: captures a screenshot of the viewer (top camera, resolution from the ScreenshotWidth and ScreenshotHeight sliders) and uses it as the value of the "MyScreenshot" image input.

- Model state source: there is no component for it, a JSON object {"type": "modelState", "props": {...}} is used. A model state of the current configuration is created and used as the value of the "MyModelState" text input, which is included in the body of the email.</item>
                  </items>
